# A supplied data Structure never executes its computed reference initializers (HG2-A, CALLFORM Р36 п.2 and rule Б).
# Self reaches its own receiver; a distinct Code writes the required data places. The launch of Writer over D2 is
# `call(D2; Writer\code)` (the body over the data), and every write into the given data is explicit (`data\seen`,
# `data\sseen`), so the values reach the data (#call-frame-20261115: no write-back of a local).
# Observation: the root values are written explicitly in sub: observe (#flush-receiver-contract).
# Step 21.7 K2, S3: the structural link carries the two given-data launches -- Code is written inside D (launched
# `D\Code()`) and Writer is written inside D2 (launched `D2\Writer()`), both over their parent; the self-launch keeps
# its `[code]` form `call(Self)`. `touch` records each of its runs in the graph (`Observed\touches`): the three
# launches add none (calls 0), and it is run once after them as the control of that record (touches 1). The bodies
# read the retained second fields (D's y 13, D2's y 23) and Self reaches its own receiver (41); every write is an
# explicit `data\` write. Observed: self_seen 41, given_seen 13, structure_seen 30, callable_seen 23.
# The former records `call(D; Code)` and `call(D2; Writer\code)` still fit the outer form [args, code] with the data
# as the args actual; the substitution of DATA is removed (the data is parent(C)), and its fields name no input of
# the parent of the code: they answer 5.
# Norm: the book #structural-call, #call-frame-20261115 (the read of a computed place executes the declaration's
# expression at the read).
Observed:
    int: self_seen 0
    int: given_seen 0
    int: structure_seen 0
    int: callable_seen 0
    int: calls 0
    int: touches 0
end: Observed
fn: touch () int
    Observed\touches := Observed\touches + 1
    return: 0
Self:
    int: x 40
    int: y 41
    @: p int Self[0]
    p := Self[1]
    int: seen 0
    Self\seen := \p
end: Self
D:
    int: x 11
    int: y 13
    Target:
        int: n 30
    end: Target
    @: p int data[touch()]
    @: s Missing
    int: seen 0
    int: sseen 0
    Code:
        @: p int data[1]
        @: s Target
        data\seen := \p
        data\sseen := s\n
    end: Code
end: D
D2:
    int: x 21
    int: y 23
    @: p int data[touch()]
    int: seen 0
    Writer:
        @: p int data[1]
        data\seen := \p
    end: Writer
end: D2
Main:
    call(Self)
    D\Code()
    D2\Writer()
    Observed\self_seen := Self\seen
    Observed\given_seen := D\seen
    Observed\structure_seen := D\sseen
    Observed\callable_seen := D2\seen
    Observed\calls := Observed\touches
    int: control touch()
